Z||000000||pHoOl||01-27-2001||12:47 PM||||Question for those of you with 87z:<P>What is the body roll like on your GTs?  I took one out for a ride yesterday, and while driving down the road i did some swerves to see how it handled.  Let me just say that it reminded me of when i had a truck.  Please tell me that there is something that is messed up with the suspension on it, because i don't have any body roll like that on my 88 GT.<P><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-27-2001||12:52 PM||||How old are the shocks and struts? If they are slightly worn it will seem a large difference from your 88. Not to mention the 88 suspension is a different design and 88 GT's have front and rear sway bars. 87's have just front sway bars. If there are tire size differences that could also add to the sway of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||01-27-2001||02:02 PM|||| 87 springs are much harder ride is hard no or little body roll I had 87se-v6 now two 88s<BR> 88 softer ride soft springs = more roll but better stick not as jumpy as 87 esp ws-6 87.<BR>sounds like normal tite 87 should be good car just not as good as 88   ray ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||01-27-2001||02:51 PM||||I had the bushings replaced last year on my 87 GT, the car still has the original suspension and there is no roll.||||reg||3
Z||000004||fiero56||01-27-2001||04:51 PM||||I've got an '86SE, I think it has softer springs than the GT, but it still has <B>way</B> more body roll than my ('88)Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-27-2001||07:36 PM||||The 88 fieros have a bigger front anti sway bar than the 87 fieros and the 88 fieros have a rear anti sway bar, the 87 fieros don't have one at all. <P>I've owned an 87 coupe with an after market rear anti sway bar and the Beretta front brake upgrade and my stock formula still handled and braked better than the coupe. The coupe would do some weird things when I pushed it to the limit while my formula feels much more stable and communicative. It goes exactly where I point it to go and I love it. I sold the coupe!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ed||01-28-2001||02:44 PM||||I have no complaints about my '87 GT with a rear sway bar and plastic sway bar bushings. Please see my comments on handling in the general forum.  ||||reg||1
